{"id": "bigearthnet_208", "source_dataset": "bigearthnet", "metadata": {}, "task": "caption", "images": [], "question": "Describe this satellite image.", "answer": "This satellite image, captured during the summer season in Austria, showcases a diverse landscape within the \"temperate, no dry season, warm summer\" climate zone. The dominant feature is the mixed forest, which covers approximately 905,000 square meters and is distributed across two large areas of 525,000 square meters and 380,000 square meters. The mixed forest shares borders with coniferous forest (~298,000 sqm), which is distributed over four individual areas, including one larger area of 236,000 square meters and three marginal areas, inland waters (~142,000 sqm), broad-leaved forest (~72,000 sqm), and arable land (~72,000 sqm). The inland waters are also adjacent to the broad-leaved forest. This complex interplay of forested areas, water bodies, and agricultural spaces highlights the varied ecosystem present in this region of Austria during the summer season."}
